  "adaptation": "Derived from public cuDNN dataGrad_cpu_ref<float> in conv_sample.cpp. Select cross-correlation, unit stride/dilation, no padding, alpha=1, beta=0, and one batch. Extend the two spatial axes to three. Invert the gather relation p = h-r, q = w-s into h = p+r, w = q+s; iterate the valid gradient/filter Cartesian product and scatter-add. This is an explicit manual reference adaptation. It changes the floating reduction order and requires the relaxed numeric model; it is not a byte-for-byte extraction of the sample. No input-dependent bounds checks remain because the output extent is gradient extent + filter extent - 1.",
